So. The mythical unspoiled ascension. We had a reasonably
well-documented one in here a while back, but the problem with getting a
perfectly documented one is that the sort of people who know the usual
NetHack communities tend to get spoiled quite quickly. And people who
try to play unspoiled tend to get spoiled /by/ other people.

A friend of mine decided to get into NetHack (having heard that it was a
famously difficult game), and we decided to try to document the entire
learning process of an unspoiled player, to see what happened. He's
playing 3.4.3 (might seem weird coming from me, but NetHack 4 changes
things round for unspoiled play to make it rather easier, and we wanted
to do things "properly"), and he's writing about his experiences here:
<http://neth4x0r.net63.net/>. I love that URL ;)

I'm helping him with technical issues (how to set up ttyrec, etc., and
how to redraw the screen if the terminal's having issues), but giving no
gameplay advice, so this should hopefully be totally unspoiled play.
Let's hope it results in an ascension!

He'd like to hear back from the community, too, so you can email
suggestions/questions/etc. to him at <neth4x0r@gmail.com>. In order to
avoid accidental spoilers, those emails are going to go to me, and I'll
forward the ones that don't contain spoilers onto him.

I look forward to this. Even if there's no eventual ascension, it should
be pretty informative for all the variant developers to know where new
players are having trouble.

